<% content_for :title, "Impulsivity & Addiction | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="addiction-impulsivity-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-hero">
    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-hero-content">

      <p class="addiction-impulsivity-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / ADDICTION / IMPULSIVITY
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>FUCK IT.</span>
        <span>JUST</span>
        <span>ONE.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="addiction-impulsivity-intro">
        YOU PICTURE ONE DRINK.<br>
        YOUR HISTORY TELLS YOU TO CONSIDER ALL TEN.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / THE DECISION -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-pink">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">01 / THE DECISION</p>

      <h2>
        IT'S<br>
        4:30<br>
        AM.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        The world outside is quiet. You’ve been up since three,
        arguing with yourself about a decision you already
        know the answer to.
      </p>

      <p>
        You count the hours, rearrange the day in your head,
        and convince yourself there’s enough time before
        a drug test. There’s doubt, but you pour anyway.
        A strong one.
      </p>

      <p>
        You binge drink alone in the dark. You know what
        this could cost you. Right now, you want out
        of your own head.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-now-later">

        <div>
          <span>WHAT YOU WANT</span>
          <p>
            Anything to take you away from this place
            for a little while.
          </p>
        </div>

        <b>VS.</b>

        <div>
          <span>WHAT YOU KNOW</span>
          <p>
            Your reasons for stopping.
            The consequences you have already experienced.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        Sometimes you spend an hour arguing yourself into it.
        Sometimes “fuck it” takes a second. Either way,
        you end up drinking before the consequences
        get a meaningful say.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / MANIA -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-yellow">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">02 / MANIA & THE SNAP DECISION</p>

      <h2>
        MAKE<br>
        IT FUCKING<br>
        STOP.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        It’s the middle of a manic episode.
        Your thoughts will not slow down,
        and you want the entire thing to stop.
      </p>

      <p>
        You want to get off the roller coaster.
        Alcohol comes to mind, and you act before giving
        the consequences much consideration.
      </p>

      <p>
        In that moment, changing how you feel becomes
        the priority. Nothing else matters—not even
        potentially going to jail.
      </p>

      <p>
        You decide to drink because you want something
        to happen now. Whatever comes afterward
        barely enters the conversation.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-cycle">
        <span>WANT IT TO STOP</span>
        <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
        <span>THINK OF ALCOHOL</span>
        <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
        <span>ACT</span>
        <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
        <span>FACE WHAT FOLLOWS</span>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / THE FUCK-ITS -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-purple">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">03 / THE FUCK-ITS</p>

      <h2>
        END THE<br>
        ARGUMENT.<br>
        POUR.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        You are tired of what is happening inside your head,
        physically to you, and around you.
        You want it interrupted.
      </p>

      <p>
        “Fuck it” lets you dismiss the reasons
        you would ordinarily take seriously.
      </p>

      <p>
        You may not have worked through those reasons
        or changed your mind about them. You have reached
        a point where you want relief badly enough
        to act without considering them.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-thoughts">
        <p>“FUCK IT.”</p>
        <p>“I JUST WANT THIS TO STOP.”</p>
        <p>“I’LL DEAL WITH IT LATER.”</p>
        <p>“JUST ONE.”</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / JUST ONE -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-black">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">04 / JUST ONE</p>

      <h2>
        ONE<br>
        BECOMES<br>
        TEN.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        “Just one” can make that decision easier.
      </p>

      <p>
        One drink sounds contained. It sounds like
        a small intervention in an experience
        you want to stop.
      </p>

      <p>
        You are picturing a limit while making the decision,
        but your own history tells you what can happen next:
        one becomes ten.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-now-later">

        <div>
          <span>THE DECISION YOU IMAGINE</span>
          <p>
            One drink. A contained choice.
            Something to interrupt the experience.
          </p>
        </div>

        <b>VS.</b>

        <div>
          <span>THE PATTERN YOU KNOW</span>
          <p>
            Continuing beyond that limit.
            Facing consequences you barely considered.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        You make the decision imagining one drink.
        Your history tells you to consider all ten.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 / CONTINUING -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-pink">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">05 / THE NEXT DECISION</p>

      <h2>
        JUST<br>
        ONE<br>
        MORE.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        The first drink creates another situation to navigate.
      </p>

      <p>
        You have already crossed the boundary you intended
        to keep, and now there is another decision
        about whether to continue.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-behaviors">

        <div>
          <span>STARTING</span>
          <p>
            “Just one” makes the first decision
            sound manageable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>CONTINUING</span>
          <p>
            “Just one more” moves the limit
            you originally imagined.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        The limit moves while the consequences accumulate.
        By the time you look back, the small decision
        you thought you were making has become
        something much larger.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 / RECOGNIZING THE LANGUAGE -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-section ai-yellow">

    <div class="addiction-impulsivity-heading">
      <p class="ai-number">06 / RECOGNIZE THE WORDS</p>

      <h2>
        HEAR<br>
        THE<br>
        SENTENCE.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ai-copy">

      <p class="ai-lead">
        The words themselves can become useful information.
      </p>

      <p>
        “Fuck it” and “just one” are familiar parts
        of your sequence. If you notice yourself saying them,
        you have something specific to report.
      </p>

      <div class="ai-friction-grid">

        <div>
          <span>“FUCK IT.”</span>
          <p>
            Notice when you start dismissing
            consequences you ordinarily take seriously.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>“JUST ONE.”</span>
          <p>
            Bring your actual history into the decision,
            including what happens after you start.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>“MAKE IT STOP.”</span>
          <p>
            Recognize the experience you need help with
            and put it into words.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>“I’M STARTING TO THINK ABOUT DRINKING.”</span>
          <p>
            Tell someone before the thought
            becomes an arrangement or an action.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p>
        “I’m starting to think about drinking to make this stop.”
        You do not have to wait until you have bought alcohol
        or started drinking before letting someone know.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="addiction-impulsivity-ending">

    <div>

      <p class="ai-ending-small">
        YOUR HISTORY BELONGS IN THE DECISION.
      </p>

      <h2>
        CONSIDER<br>
        ALL<br>
        <span>TEN.</span>
      </h2>

    </div>

    <div class="ai-ending-copy">

      <p>
        Accountability means being honest about what happens
        when you start. “Just one” has repeatedly become ten.
        You know that now, and it belongs in the decision
        before you pour.
      </p>

      <p>
        You can understand how desperately you wanted
        the experience to stop and still acknowledge
        what drinking cost you.
      </p>

      <p>
        That understanding gives you something specific
        to plan for—and something to tell another person
        before you are alone in the dark
        making the same argument again.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO ADDICTION",
          addiction_path,
          class: "ai-back-button" %>

    </div>

  </section>

</main>